+RWFP_62=USB 3.0 signalling radiates into the 2.4 GHz band. Enabling this runs the USB ports at USB 2.0 speed.
+RWFP_63=Enable (USB ports at 2.0 speed)
+RWFP_64=Disable (full USB 3.0 speed)
+RWFP_65=Disconnect a client whose signal drops below the threshold so it can move to a stronger AP or node. Off, or -90 to -40 dBm.
+RWFP_66=Auto channel options
+RWDN_102=What the block count means
+RWDN_103=Blocked packets is every packet Warden dropped - inbound, outbound and the router's own traffic, IPv4 and IPv6 - counted since the date shown under the country table. The live counters are banked to internal flash every 15 minutes and on every apply, so the number survives reboots and rule rebuilds.
+RWDN_104=It counts packets, not connection attempts. A blocked scanner retries each SYN several times and a LAN device keeps retrying a blocked destination for a minute, so one attempt can add dozens.
+RWDN_105=The log is a different view: one line per dropped packet, only while Warden logging is on, kept in a small rotating syslog buffer. The Firewall page's Logging tab shows the last 400 lines, mixed with the stock firewall's own entries.
+RWDN_106=Under a burst the kernel and syslog drop lines while the counter keeps every packet, so the count is always the larger figure and the reliable one.
+RWDN_107=Countries, threat feeds and manual blocks are read from the same snapshot as the total, so they add up to it. A remainder shows as Unclassified only for statistics saved by an older firmware.
+RWDN_108=Blocked packets
